1
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,800
Ever since the day
I found out you were married,

2
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:04,560
I've never dared cross the line.

3
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:06,120
I came here today

4
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,760
so you could rest easy.

5
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,000
I think of Runch as a friend.

6
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,840
What I did was wrong.
I'll treat you better.

7
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,840
- I just need a roof over my head.
- No…

8
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,240
- What? Honey!
- Mom!

9
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:17,280
- Ging!
- Mom!

10
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:20,280
You think you can fool me
by pretending to be nice?

11
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:25,840
I'll have to show Runch
her mom's true colors.

12
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,040
This is a war between a wife
and her mother-in-law.

13
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:29,840
Yeah.

14
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,240
Ms. Runch! Hello.

15
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:36,960
You arrived just in time.

16
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,960
Ms. Neen is inside. You may go in now.

17
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,160
She's not in a very good mood, though.
So please beware.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,840
Is something wrong?

19
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:47,680
It's about work.
Something didn't go her way.

20
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,280
Okay.

21
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:54,200
I bought two cakes. One's for you,

22
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,600
and please plate the other one for Neen.

23
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,840
As for her tea, I'll bring it myself.

24
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:03,760
Got it. Thank you kindly for the dessert.

25
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,520
My pleasure.

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,320
Yes, Nat?

27
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,000
Runch!

28
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:37,560
Nat told me her boss
is in a bad mood today.

29
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:41,440
I hope my flowers

30
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,240
can cheer you up.

31
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,800
Aw.

32
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,680
They sure help.

33
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:51,080
Smell so good too.

34
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:55,760
Not as good as you, though.
You smell really good.

35
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,880
Does that mean

36
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,440
you're feeling better now?

37
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,600
Just seeing your face is enough.

38
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,960
- Is this mine?
- Yeah.

39
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:13,720
There's cake too.
I asked Nat to plate it for you.

40
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,160
How suspicious.

41
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,600
Why'd you buy me
so much stuff all of a sudden?

42
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,440
Is it some kind of special day?
I can't remember.

43
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,560
I just wanted to.

44
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:41,880
Here you go.

45
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,760
Please go ahead and feed each other.

46
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:46,600
I'm fine eating alone.

47
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:48,120
Don't worry.

48
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:51,120
I'll hook you up with guys and girls
here and there in our office.

49
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,840
Whoa! No, thank you.

50
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,360
No one's my type, though.

51
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,240
Yet you complain that you're single.
You're so picky.

52
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,200
Well, Ms. Runch comes to see you often.

53
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,960
Anyone who's single would get jealous.

54
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,320
Nat, if you're done with work for the day,

55
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,960
you may go home.

56
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,040
Okay. See you tomorrow.

57
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,000
Okay.

58
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,600
Come here.

59
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,040
So good.

60
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,920
Did I get some on my face?

61
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,520
What's wrong?

62
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,320
You're so pretty.

63
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,520
- Runch.
- Yes?

64
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,800
Can I ask you something?

65
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:04,520
When your mom asked to stay at our place,

66
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,080
she wasn't scheming anything, right?

67
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,080
I don't think so.

68
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,320
Really?

69
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:20,000
It's probably typical of an old woman
who's upset with her husband.

70
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,160
Hello, Mom.

71
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:34,720
Dinner? Sure.

72
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,920
Yes, I'm free. I'll bring Runch too.

73
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,200
Okay. See you later.

74
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,040
Sure. See you.

75
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,520
Bye.

76
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:49,640
Let me call my mom and tell her

77
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,240
we'll be home late tonight.

78
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,240
Sure.

79
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,120
They're all Runch's favorites.

80
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:01,920
I bet she'll love them.

81
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,960
Runch.

82
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,320
You're having dinner
at Neen's parents' place?

83
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,360
Of course. Please go ahead.

84
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,480
Please tell everyone I miss them.

85
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,320
Eat up, Runch.

86
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,760
Thank you, Neen.

87
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,560
Here.

88
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,320
You eat up too.

89
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,040
Thank you.

90
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:06,360
Hey. You got some on your face.
Let me get that for you.

91
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:12,120
It's the sauce. Right there.

92
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:26,040
There. Beautiful.

93
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:28,360
Thank you, my gorgeous wife.

94
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:31,680
My pleasure.

95
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:42,320
Hold on. Is there something we don't know?

96
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:46,600
Yeah. Are you two really being lovebirds,

97
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,520
or is this just an act?

98
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,560
Runch,

99
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,160
would you tell everyone?

100
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:02,680
We've talked about it.

101
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,320
We agreed to stay married.

102
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,040
- Yes, we did!
- Really?

103
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:12,400
- Yes.
- We decided to stay together.

104
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:17,480
I'm so happy to hear that.

105
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:21,040
- That's fantastic. Right, honey?
- I'm happy too, honey.

106
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,480
I really am.

107
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:26,160
We'll finally be a real family.

108
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,640
Way to go, my sister-in-law.

109
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,799
- I'm very proud of you.
- Yeah.

110
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:36,240
Dad, I think we should celebrate tonight.

111
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,880
Sure!

112
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:41,280
- You can't go home until you're drunk.
- Yeah!

113
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,520
Nai, not again!

114
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,720
It's only occasionally,

115
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:45,440
- so it's fine.
- He's right.

116
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,880
Don't be shy.

117
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,880
- Go all out.
- Are you kidding me, Dad?

118
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,440
Don't drink, honey.

119
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,760
Ugh, Neen.

120
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,960
I think you got some on your lips.

121
00:08:58,040 --> 00:09:00,040
Aw, honey.

122
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,920
Come on.

123
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,280
Let's celebrate, Dad.

124
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,760
Cheers.

125
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,080
Cheers.

126
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,320
Why don't you join them?

127
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:20,080
No, thanks.

128
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:23,080
If I get drunk, who will drive us home?

129
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:26,160
If you can't drive,
just stay the night here.

130
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:29,280
Runch will probably refuse.

131
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,360
Why?

132
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,880
Her mother's been staying with us.

133
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,600
What?

134
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:38,320
Sounds like a disaster.

135
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,720
Not yet.

136
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,680
It's so quiet, actually.

137
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,080
So unusually quiet.

138
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:46,480
She's been behaving really well.

139
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,680
But…?

140
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:58,000
But I know it's fake.
I know she's pretending.

141
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,640
So what are you going to do?

142
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,480
What I can do for now…

143
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:14,080
is to do whatever it takes

144
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,760
for her mom to show her true colors.

145
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,040
Just don't be too harsh.

146
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,640
I feel bad for Runch.

147
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:25,480
She's still her mother, after all.
There's no cutting her off…

148
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,680
no matter what her mother's like.

149
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,480
I know. That's the hardest part.

150
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,480
Come on. Walk.

151
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,000
- Hey, wait.
- Mom.

152
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,320
What happened, Runch?

153
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,240
- Mom.
- You're so drunk!

154
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:50,160
She's probably happy,

155
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,680
so she had quite a few.

156
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,960
This is what you call "a few"?

157
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Runch.

158
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,560
- Mom!
- Yeah?

159
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,840
Why are you still up?

160
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:02,600
I was waiting for you to come home.

161
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,680
Why would you wait?

162
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:10,120
I'm all grown up now. I'm not a child.

163
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:13,520
You'll always be a child to me.

164
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,560
No matter what you do,
I'll always worry about you.

165
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,680
But…

166
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,680
- Runch?
- Hey.

167
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:22,960
Runch!

168
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:24,520
No!

169
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:29,880
Runch.

170
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,120
Good night, Mom.

171
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,040
Come on.

172
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:46,120
Good night.

173
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:25,360
Here.

174
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,880
Some hot ginger tea for Runch.

175
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,520
It'll help with her nausea.

176
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:36,240
Thank you, Mom.
But she's so drunk she fell asleep.

177
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,800
Is this the way your family does things?

178
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,600
What do you mean?

179
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:45,080
You only brought her home
after she got that drunk.

180
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:50,600
She's all grown up now, Mom.

181
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:53,760
Plus, she had a really good time today.

182
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:56,240
I don't want to stop her all the time.

183
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,800
But as a wife, taking her home
isn't the only way to take care of her.

184
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,720
I take care of her
whichever way she wants me to,

185
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,400
not just the way someone else sees fit.

186
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,400
I'm just worried about my daughter.

187
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:19,080
Runch never used to drink this much
while she was with me.

188
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:24,120
Maybe she didn't have the courage
to live life the way she wanted yet.

189
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:29,200
I raised her myself. I should know best

190
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:32,280
what's good for her and what's not.

191
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,520
I believe you.

192
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:37,240
And I know how much you love her.

193
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:43,240
But now, I am the one
who lives together with her

194
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,640
every day.

195
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,280
What's that noise, Runch?

196
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,120
Mom! Mom!

197
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:54,000
Mom!

198
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,920
Mom.

199
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,480
Mom!

200
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:09,520
Oh! Up already, honey?

201
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:12,000
Your vacuuming woke us up, Mom.

202
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:14,480
Ah! Oh dear. I'm sorry.

203
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,160
It's just that I woke up early

204
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:18,880
and I didn't want to lie in bed.
I wanted to do something,

205
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,480
so I figured I should
clean the house a bit.

206
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:23,800
Actually, you didn't have to.

207
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,560
The maid will be here anyway.

208
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:28,160
That won't do, Runch. I'm staying here,

209
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:31,480
and I don't want to just sit around
doing nothing every day.

210
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,640
I want to help.
I don't want to be a burden.

211
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:44,960
Mom?

212
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:47,920
What's this?

213
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:55,040
That's a photo of me and Runch.
I brought it along.

214
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,800
I just love this photo.

215
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,560
That's why I wanted to put it here.

216
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:02,080
Why didn't you put it in your room?

217
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:05,640
I think this is a good spot, though. Here.

218
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,360
See? It's a common area.

219
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,640
Your guests will see it too.

220
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:14,320
You're right! Anyone who enters the house

221
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:18,400
will see these and be able to tell
who Runch is happier with.

222
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,640
You're right!

223
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,640
You're right, Neen.

224
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,400
What's with the outfits?

225
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:54,920
We're treating ourselves
to your favorite restaurant.

226
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,440
I'll book us a table.

227
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:02,160
I don't think we can today.

228
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,680
Why not?

229
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:08,200
Well, my mom's cooking.

230
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,240
Let's eat in today.

231
00:17:14,079 --> 00:17:16,280
We can eat out another day.

232
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:17,240
Okay?

233
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:19,520
Please?

234
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,920
Sure.

235
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:31,360
Then I'm helping her out.

236
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,440
Can I help you with anything?

237
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:04,560
Should I chop something up?

238
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,760
Can you chop the chicken
on the cutting board?

239
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,160
So sorry, Mom.

240
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:30,000
Alright. Now that we're alone together,

241
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:34,120
why don't you just tell me what you want?

242
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:37,360
I should ask you the same thing.

243
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:42,120
You picked a fight with your husband

244
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:45,440
and faked being sad
in order to move in with us, right?

245
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:54,120
No answer. That means I was right.

246
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,320
You're so smart.

247
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,880
I'll be honest with you.

248
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:14,200
I'll do whatever it takes
to get you out of Runch's life.

249
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:20,160
Do whatever you want.
Runch will choose me anyway, Mom.

250
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:22,400
Sure.

251
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,760
Then let's have a cooking competition.

252
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:28,360
Let's see who Runch will choose.

253
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:32,200
Game on, Mom.

254
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,840
This kind of dish takes
good understanding to cook,

255
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:24,320
not just a recipe.

256
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:28,760
True. Being with her every day taught me
how to season certain dishes right.

257
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:40,960
Smells amazing! What are you making?

258
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:44,080
Neen and I are cooking together.

259
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:47,080
Yeah. It's so much fun.

260
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:48,880
Look.

261
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,760
I made salted fish fried rice.

262
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:52,880
Your childhood favorite dish.

263
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:54,120
As for me,

264
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:57,240
I made you truffle pasta.
You said it was your comfort food.

265
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:59,600
Lucky me!

266
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:01,480
I get to eat two very good dishes.

267
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,240
- Yes!
- Yes!

268
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,840
- Dig in.
- Dig in.

269
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:44,200
What's wrong, Runch?

270
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:45,720
It's so salty!

271
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:05,200
It really is!

272
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:27,040
What, Runch?

273
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:30,320
This one's salty too.

274
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,680
Is it?

275
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,120
Why is it so salty?

276
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:56,240
All in all, everything's delicious.

277
00:23:56,320 --> 00:24:00,480
It just takes a little imagination.

278
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:08,320
Here you go, Neen,

279
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,400
Runch. I packed you some lunch.

280
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,760
It's to compensate for how
I didn't cook well yesterday.

281
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:16,600
I don't want to bother you.

282
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,560
It was no bother.

283
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:21,080
I made it for you both.

284
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,600
I put my heart into it.

285
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:27,280
You two can share it. And let me know
if you ever want something in particular.

286
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:30,360
I'll gladly make you anything.

287
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:31,480
Okay, Mom.

288
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:36,680
Let's go.

289
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:39,040
I'd better get to work.

290
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,080
See you.

291
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:42,880
Enjoy your lunch.

292
00:24:42,960 --> 00:24:44,080
Of course.

293
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:52,840
Neen.

294
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:58,200
You should give it to your coworkers.

295
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:03,960
Why? My mom made it for you.

296
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:06,400
Is it okay if I refuse her kindness?

297
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:09,280
To be honest, I don't trust your mom.

298
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,760
But Neen,

299
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:14,360
my mom's trying to be a better person.

300
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:16,440
It's clearly an act.

301
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:17,760
Neen.

302
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:20,440
Don't. It's too early
for us to be fighting.

303
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,760
I'm not picking a fight.

304
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:29,040
I just wish you'd give her a chance.

305
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:32,160
Can I not?

306
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:35,200
Whatever. I'm off to work.
See you in the evening.

307
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,120
Neen, you're home!

308
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:03,880
What's all this?

309
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,640
They're plants and trees.
Don't you know what they are?

310
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:10,360
I know what they are,
but why'd you bring so many?

311
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:13,280
Well, they're all lucky plants.

312
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:17,400
The canna lily brings peace to the family.

313
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:18,880
This one,

314
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:22,840
the water jasmine, protects us from evil.

315
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:28,320
The tamarind tree wards off evil spirits.

316
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,800
This way, our house
will be free of bad luck.

317
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:32,480
What do you think?

318
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:35,920
You're the bad luck in this house.

319
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:39,080
Oh my! Why would you say that to me?

320
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,640
Isn't it true, though?

321
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:43,840
Runch isn't here, Mom.
So you can drop the act.

322
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:47,520
There's no way I'd believe
you can really change.

323
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:49,720
Neen,

324
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:53,240
let's be reasonable here.
Why get emotional?

325
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:56,320
I really am trying to treat you better.

326
00:26:57,560 --> 00:27:00,240
Stop putting on an act already, Mom.
It's making me sick.

327
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:02,800
Why do you have to be so mean?

328
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:06,360
I know

329
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:09,880
I've wronged you. That's why you hate me.

330
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:13,400
But now, I really do feel bad about it.

331
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:17,360
I don't believe you,
and there's no way I will.

332
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:20,760
Get all those trees out of here.
I don't like them.

333
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:24,840
Neen, Neen!

334
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:27,840
Don't go yet! Please listen to me, honey.

335
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:30,040
Please listen to me!

336
00:27:30,720 --> 00:27:32,120
Neen!

337
00:27:35,520 --> 00:27:37,600
NEW RECORDING 5

338
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:42,600
I'm always one step ahead of you,
you naive girl.

339
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:54,000
What?

340
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:55,840
Why are you sitting outside?

341
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:58,080
I'm too scared to go inside.

342
00:27:58,680 --> 00:28:00,800
Why? What happened?

343
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:09,800
Oh, Runch! Why are you home so late?
I've been waiting to have dinner with you.

344
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:11,120
I'm starving.

345
00:28:11,640 --> 00:28:13,920
Did you have a fight with Mom?

346
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:22,560
Did that old hag say something?

347
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:27,600
Neen. Don't call my mom that.

348
00:28:27,680 --> 00:28:29,000
That's not very nice.

349
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:33,200
So what did she say I did? Tell me.

350
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:38,080
Well, it's about the plants and trees.

351
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:43,080
My mom means well.
She just wants to bring us good luck.

352
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:47,960
- Please let her plant them.
- Did she really tell on me over that?

353
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:51,040
She didn't. She was just
telling me about it.

354
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:53,680
You know, she really cares
about what you think.

355
00:28:53,760 --> 00:28:54,880
Really?

356
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:56,520
This shows that she cares?

357
00:28:56,600 --> 00:28:59,080
If she really cared,
she should've asked me

358
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:01,280
before planting them at our place.

359
00:29:02,800 --> 00:29:06,360
Whatever. She can plant
whatever she wants. I don't care anymore.

360
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:09,400
- Don't be mad, Neen.
- Of course I am.

361
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:10,640
I'm so mad.

362
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:14,280
Whenever things don't get her way,
she tells on me to you. I hate that.

363
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:17,360
We're all grown-ups here. We aren't kids.

364
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,680
Well, I'm sorry on her behalf.

365
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:23,680
Your mom's the one who should apologize,
not you.

366
00:29:25,040 --> 00:29:26,440
I'm done with this conversation.

367
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:28,640
Okay, okay.

368
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:31,560
I'll stop. Let's have dinner, shall we?

369
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:34,800
I'm not hungry anymore. I'm not eating.

370
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:58,240
Hello.

371
00:29:58,320 --> 00:30:01,120
Oh, hello. Uh…

372
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:02,760
I'm Runchlaphat's mother.

373
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:06,040
You mean Ms. Runch, the beautiful lawyer?

374
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:08,440
Yes, that's her.

375
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:10,480
I've been staying at her place lately.

376
00:30:12,760 --> 00:30:14,560
Why don't we talk inside?

377
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:18,880
That's for you to take home.

378
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:21,320
Thank you.

379
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:24,800
My daughter works hard.
Some days she comes home late.

380
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:27,040
That's why I usually cook her something.

381
00:30:27,120 --> 00:30:29,960
It's better than eating out
at restaurants.

382
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:31,520
Those foods are full of MSG.

383
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:38,320
Doesn't Ms. Runch's wife cook for her?

384
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:43,560
Don't get me started.
Neen doesn't really do any of that.

385
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:46,040
But I can't blame her.

386
00:30:46,120 --> 00:30:49,040
I get that she's busy with work.
But even so,

387
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:51,520
she'll go out to party with her friends
and get home late,

388
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:54,040
and my daughter
would have to take care of her.

389
00:30:56,840 --> 00:30:58,320
Please try it.

390
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,920
I'm not that good a cook,

391
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,160
but I do try my best for my daughter.

392
00:31:02,680 --> 00:31:04,120
How sweet.

393
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:07,040
Ms. Runch sure is lucky
to have a mother like you.

394
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:11,520
It's all I can do as a mother.

395
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:21,040
Wake up.

396
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:24,600
What's up?

397
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:26,760
Come on.

398
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:29,080
Let's go work out.

399
00:31:30,240 --> 00:31:33,000
- Let's go.
- No. Let me sleep.

400
00:31:37,560 --> 00:31:40,080
Neen, are you still mad at me?

401
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:50,880
That's enough.

402
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,200
No, it's not.

403
00:31:53,760 --> 00:31:55,840
Not until you forgive me.

404
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:02,520
Okay, okay! I give up!

405
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:04,960
Do you forgive me yet?

406
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,680
Fine, I forgive you.

407
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:10,640
You really are something.

408
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:14,120
Come on.

409
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:17,080
Let's go exercise, shall we?

410
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:33,600
Come on. Up.

411
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:35,400
Yay!

412
00:32:35,480 --> 00:32:37,280
Let's go!

413
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:45,600
Why are you smiling?

414
00:32:46,880 --> 00:32:48,680
Did you forget something?

415
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,160
What?

416
00:32:59,240 --> 00:33:00,560
This.

417
00:33:01,120 --> 00:33:02,600
I almost forgot.

418
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:06,480
How could you? It means so much to us.

419
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:09,200
It's crazy to think

420
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:12,880
that we'll be each other's wives
in just a few months.

421
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:14,120
Yeah.

422
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:17,120
We've almost been together for two years.

423
00:33:17,200 --> 00:33:19,360
Time flies, doesn't it?

424
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:20,560
It sure does.

425
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:24,000
Neen.

426
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:28,760
What's that, Runch?

427
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:32,400
What?

428
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:45,280
They're watches.

429
00:33:46,280 --> 00:33:48,200
But they're not meant

430
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:51,920
to tell how much time has passed.

431
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:56,720
Instead, they'll remind me
that with every step I take,

432
00:33:56,800 --> 00:33:58,560
you'll always be there with me.

433
00:33:59,720 --> 00:34:02,840
How sweet. Thank you, Runch.

434
00:34:04,280 --> 00:34:05,600
Can you help me put it on?

435
00:34:06,600 --> 00:34:09,080
Of course. Here.

436
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:17,960
There.

437
00:34:18,040 --> 00:34:19,040
Ready?

438
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:21,960
Now we can jog together.

439
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:23,480
Let's go.

440
00:34:29,760 --> 00:34:30,960
Runch!

441
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:36,040
- Are you good?
- Yeah.

442
00:34:36,880 --> 00:34:38,600
I'm getting thirsty.

443
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:42,679
Can you get me some water?

444
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:44,679
Of course.

445
00:34:45,199 --> 00:34:46,520
I'll be right back.

446
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:47,520
Okay.

447
00:34:47,600 --> 00:34:51,320
See? Just like Ms. Runch's mother said.

448
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:54,000
- What did she say?
- Oh,

449
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:55,960
she said she doesn't
take care of her wife.

450
00:34:56,040 --> 00:34:59,360
See? She's thirsty, but instead
of getting her own water,

451
00:34:59,440 --> 00:35:00,720
she's making her wife do it.

452
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:04,160
That's not how a good wife should be.

453
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:05,600
Exactly.

454
00:35:05,680 --> 00:35:08,920
She just sits back
and lets her wife do everything.

455
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,200
That's why Runch's mother cooks for her,

456
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:13,480
otherwise she'd have nothing good to eat.

457
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,000
- Really?
- Yeah.

458
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:23,920
Oh, Neen.

459
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:25,560
So thirsty you couldn't wait, huh?

460
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:27,160
Did you badmouth me to my neighbors?

461
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:31,080
What are you talking about?
I don't understand.

462
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:33,000
Stop acting so innocent.

463
00:35:33,080 --> 00:35:35,480
What'd you say to make them think
I don't take care of Runch?

464
00:35:36,680 --> 00:35:39,520
I didn't. Don't lie about me like that.

465
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:43,000
Lie about you? I heard
what they said with my own ears!

466
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:44,040
Say you did it!

467
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:45,920
- Come on, say it!
- Neen!

468
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Neen, let go. You're hurting me.

469
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:50,840
Neen, please let go of her.
You're hurting her for real.

470
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:53,960
I won't let go
until your mom tells the truth.

471
00:35:54,040 --> 00:35:55,960
Stop bullshitting me! Stop it!

472
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:57,960
- Stop it!
- Neen, that's enough!

473
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:08,120
Did you just yell at me?

474
00:36:10,040 --> 00:36:11,280
I'm sorry.

475
00:36:13,160 --> 00:36:16,720
I didn't mean to, but you wouldn't listen.

476
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:19,720
You say I wouldn't listen,
but you wouldn't either.

477
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,760
Or do you think I was lying?

478
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:30,320
Okay.

479
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:34,680
Then you can stay with her all you want.

480
00:36:36,960 --> 00:36:38,560
Neen, wait--

481
00:36:42,600 --> 00:36:43,640
Mom.

482
00:36:44,600 --> 00:36:48,080
Runch, just go after her.
Don't worry about me.

483
00:36:49,080 --> 00:36:51,240
How could I go when you're like this?

484
00:36:52,520 --> 00:36:54,160
I'll get you an inhaler.

485
00:36:55,040 --> 00:36:56,040
Okay, honey.

486
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:11,400
You just told me you're staying married,

487
00:37:11,480 --> 00:37:14,160
and now you had such a bad fight
you ran away from home?

488
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:16,720
Well, Runch was the one
who was being unreasonable.

489
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:20,880
But from what you told me,
you went too far.

490
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:23,760
You insulted her mother.
How could she not be upset?

491
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:26,240
What? It was her fault, though.

492
00:37:26,320 --> 00:37:29,480
I don't like being accused
when I didn't do anything wrong.

493
00:37:29,560 --> 00:37:32,760
So what are you going to do?
Stay here and not go home?

494
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:33,960
Yes.

495
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:39,040
I won't go home until her mother leaves.

496
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:44,120
What good will all these outbursts do?

497
00:37:44,200 --> 00:37:45,480
I don't know.

498
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:54,400
<i>Runch,</i>

499
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:56,880
<i>I don't want to blame your mom, but,</i>

500
00:37:56,960 --> 00:38:00,360
<i>recording her conversation with Neen</i>
<i>so she could play it back to you?</i>

501
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:02,160
<i>That doesn't seem natural at all.</i>

502
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:03,560
What do you mean?

503
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:05,760
<i>Have you ever seen a soap opera?</i>

504
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:08,320
This is exactly like a soap opera plot.

505
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:10,120
It's as if your mom had planned it,

506
00:38:10,200 --> 00:38:13,120
trying to make Neen
look like the bad guy to you.

507
00:38:13,760 --> 00:38:16,120
<i>Would my mom really go that far?</i>

508
00:38:18,080 --> 00:38:20,880
Mothers will do anything,

509
00:38:20,960 --> 00:38:24,040
especially one
who's as protective as yours.

510
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:27,520
<i>She'd do it just so she wouldn't</i>
<i>lose you to someone else.</i>

511
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:31,200
<i>I think you fell for your mother's trick.</i>

512
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:35,000
<i>You'd better apologize to Neen</i>
<i>and win her back.</i>

513
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,400
Hello, Dad.

514
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:46,880
Hello, Mom.

515
00:38:46,960 --> 00:38:47,800
Hello.

516
00:38:49,240 --> 00:38:50,800
Hello, Nai.

517
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:55,600
You see, I came here to--

518
00:38:55,680 --> 00:38:59,440
Runch, you don't have to say anything.
I know what happened.

519
00:39:05,560 --> 00:39:08,440
Does… Does everyone know already?

520
00:39:11,600 --> 00:39:14,880
It's not that hard to guess what happened.

521
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:26,080
I'm sorry for yelling at Neen.

522
00:39:27,960 --> 00:39:32,200
Fighting is just part of a relationship.

523
00:39:37,720 --> 00:39:40,160
It doesn't matter whether you fight.

524
00:39:41,240 --> 00:39:43,800
What matters is whether
you still choose each other

525
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:46,280
after you fight.

526
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:53,880
I choose her.

527
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:56,640
I always have.

528
00:39:57,600 --> 00:40:00,320
But sometimes,
I'm not so good at handling it.

529
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:07,120
Neen's in her room.
You should go and see her.

530
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:13,040
Okay.

531
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:21,400
Neen. Can you open the door for me?

532
00:40:27,120 --> 00:40:28,400
Neen,

533
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:32,320
I know you're listening.

534
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:37,480
I've come to take you home.

535
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:44,760
I'm not going.

536
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:47,560
I'm sorry.

537
00:40:52,680 --> 00:40:55,960
I don't want to hear your apology.
Those are nothing but words.

538
00:40:56,520 --> 00:40:59,720
I want you to show me you're really sorry.

539
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:10,560
What do you want me to do?

540
00:41:14,160 --> 00:41:16,440
Do whatever it takes
to make your mom leave,

541
00:41:16,520 --> 00:41:18,680
then I'll accept your apology.

542
00:41:38,520 --> 00:41:41,640
How'd it go, Runch?
Did she agree to come home?

543
00:41:43,560 --> 00:41:44,880
No.

544
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:45,960
Oh dear.

545
00:41:46,040 --> 00:41:48,240
She's still mad at me, isn't she?

546
00:41:51,520 --> 00:41:55,360
It's my fault.
I'm the one who caused this.

547
00:41:55,440 --> 00:41:58,680
Had I not moved in and just stayed away,

548
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:01,520
Neen wouldn't have been so mad at you.

549
00:42:02,160 --> 00:42:05,200
I'm getting too old.
I didn't think it through,

550
00:42:05,280 --> 00:42:07,240
and now I'm giving you a hard time.

551
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:12,800
Mom.

552
00:42:15,400 --> 00:42:17,280
Please don't say that.

553
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:21,480
Should I make up with her?

554
00:42:21,560 --> 00:42:24,320
I'll go and apologize.
I'll even bow down to her

555
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:26,920
as long as she'll move back in with you.

556
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:31,200
It's okay. I'll handle this myself.

557
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:33,360
I'm worried, though.

558
00:42:33,440 --> 00:42:36,080
I'm scared she won't be back ever again.

559
00:42:39,440 --> 00:42:41,880
I won't give up so easily, Mom.

560
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:46,480
I'll find a way to make up with her
and win her back.

561
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:52,000
No matter how hard it is,
I won't let go of her hand.

562
00:42:53,080 --> 00:42:54,840
I believe in you, Runch.

563
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:49,840
‪ONE YEAR AGO

564
00:43:58,240 --> 00:44:00,400
Finally, the day has come.

565
00:44:01,880 --> 00:44:04,400
The day we become each other's wives.

566
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:15,640
And from this day forward,

567
00:44:16,960 --> 00:44:20,480
we'll be each other's wives forever.

568
00:44:24,360 --> 00:44:25,520
Yes, we will.

569
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:01,920
You threw away my ring, didn't you?

570
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:03,720
So that ring matters more than me?

571
00:45:03,800 --> 00:45:06,080
Couldn't keep up the act,
so you finally snapped?

572
00:45:06,160 --> 00:45:07,680
This was your plan, wasn't it?

573
00:45:07,760 --> 00:45:11,080
I'm an innocent girl.
I'd never scheme against you.

574
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:12,040
You're so full of it!

575
00:45:12,120 --> 00:45:13,640
- Huh?
- Mom!

576
00:45:13,720 --> 00:45:15,960
- That's enough. Mom!
- You!

577
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:18,320
Stop it! Don't you lay a finger on Neen.

578
00:45:18,400 --> 00:45:19,640
Don't hurt her.

579
00:45:19,720 --> 00:45:22,160
I know it must be difficult for you.

580
00:45:22,240 --> 00:45:24,600
If you want to talk or vent…

581
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:27,600
<i>…I'm always here to listen.</i>

582
00:45:28,200 --> 00:45:31,960
Getting to hug you
is enough to cheer me up.

583
00:46:14,960 --> 00:46:16,960
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
